#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541328 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4cac0cfd-8c08-5693-8241-6ca20d9e2a35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541297} {:answer/id #uuid "6757bd50-9e6f-5dd8-a9f2-cedca3d927b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "54" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541311} {:answer/id #uuid "98bec14f-3a08-5435-93a8-37c729d5ad2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541322} {:answer/id #uuid "ee26e376-13fa-58e3-8df2-d79974758cc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541341} {:answer/id #uuid "eeb45e08-511b-5b14-94c9-f0ceacb890e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541342}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541342} :answer-field/id #uuid "addb0864-1aef-5c00-9c38-d91ca6be4e91" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541331}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a23caed0-b0d6-5bc7-85a1-57147c01f56c" :question/problem "Use the change of variables \n\n$$\nu=3 x - 2 y,\\quad v=y + 2 z,\\quad w=2 z\n$$\n\nto evaluate the triple integral\n\n$$\n\\iiint_R \\left(\\left(3 x - 2 y\\right) \\left(y + 2 z\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}V,\n$$\n\n \nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z):0\\le 3 x - 2 y\\le 1,\\quad 0\\le y + 2 z\\le 3,\\quad 0\\le z\\le 2\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uvw$-space to our region $R$ in the $xyz$-space.\n\nTo compute the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\text{ }dV={∭}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v,w),y(u,v,w),z(u,v,w))\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nNote that the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=3 x - 2 y,\\quad v=y + 2 z,\\quad w=2 z\n$$\n\ngives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}u(x,y,z) \\\\ v(x,y,z) \\\\ w(x,y,z)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo compute the required integral, we proceed in four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $R$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nOur domain in the $uvw$-space is\n\n$$\n\\Delta=\\{(u,v,w):0\\le u\\le 1,\\quad 0\\le v\\le 3,\\quad 0\\le w\\le 4\\}.\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial(u,v,w)}{\\partial(x,y,z)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial z} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial z} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial z}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\left(2\\right)(-1)^{3+3}\\begin{vmatrix}3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\left(2\\right)\\left(\\left(3\\right)\\cdot \\left(1\\right)-\\left(-2\\right)\\cdot \\left(0\\right)\\right) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial(x,y,z)}{\\partial(u,v,w)}=\\left(\\frac{\\partial(u,v,w)}{\\partial(x,y,z)}\\right)^{-1}=\\frac{1}{6}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Perform the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iiint_R \\left(\\left(3 x - 2 y\\right) \\left(y + 2 z\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}V & =\\iiint_\\Delta \\left(u v\\right)\\cdot \\left|\\frac{1}{6}\\right|\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\mathrm{d}v\\mathrm{d}w \\\\  & =\\iiint_\\Delta \\left(\\frac{u v}{6}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\mathrm{d}v\\mathrm{d}w \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\int_{0}^{3}\\int_{0}^{4}\\left(\\frac{u v}{6}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}w\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\int_{0}^{3}\\left(\\left[\\frac{u v w}{6}\\right]_{w=0}^{w=4}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\int_{0}^{3}\\left(\\left(\\frac{u v \\left(4\\right)}{6}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{u v \\left(0\\right)}{6}\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\int_{0}^{3}\\left(\\left(\\frac{2 u v}{3}\\right)-\\left(0\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\int_{0}^{3}\\left(\\frac{2 u v}{3}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(\\left[\\frac{u v^{2}}{3}\\right]_{v=0}^{v=3}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(\\left(\\frac{u \\left(3\\right)^{2}}{3}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{u \\left(0\\right)^{2}}{3}\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(\\left(3 u\\right)-\\left(0\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(3 u\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\left[\\frac{3 u^{2}}{2}\\right]_{u=0}^{u=1} \\\\  & =\\left(\\frac{3 \\left(1\\right)^{2}}{2}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{3 \\left(0\\right)^{2}}{2}\\right) \\\\  & =\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)-\\left(0\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541332 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08d7f614-2d0d-5b4f-8a4d-5a430e668c3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541277} {:answer/id #uuid "152b9c08-7c4c-5e4f-a8bf-bbdc2a3842c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541279} {:answer/id #uuid "24a04031-d6cc-50a4-b638-5f6376be444c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541286} {:answer/id #uuid "5a177f47-6fb8-5c2f-9bfa-96bcc20a72cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541304} {:answer/id #uuid "5d07125f-13b1-5f8d-a78d-d9b4fa23d612" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{24}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541306}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541286} :answer-field/id #uuid "ccb3f74c-54d7-51d7-81f2-a0054fada802" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541335}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b5692f69-3609-5609-944f-4e446bbb7794" :question/problem "Use the change of variables \n\n$$\nu=- 3 x + 2 y,\\quad v=y - 2 z,\\quad w=2 z\n$$\n\nto evaluate the triple integral\n\n$$\n\\iiint_R \\left(\\left(- 3 x + 2 y\\right) \\left(y - 2 z\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}V,\n$$\n\n \nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z):0\\le - 3 x + 2 y\\le 1,\\quad 0\\le y - 2 z\\le 1,\\quad 0\\le z\\le 1\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uvw$-space to our region $R$ in the $xyz$-space.\n\nTo compute the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\text{ }dV={∭}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v,w),y(u,v,w),z(u,v,w))\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nNote that the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=- 3 x + 2 y,\\quad v=y - 2 z,\\quad w=2 z\n$$\n\ngives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}u(x,y,z) \\\\ v(x,y,z) \\\\ w(x,y,z)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo compute the required integral, we proceed in four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $R$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nOur domain in the $uvw$-space is\n\n$$\n\\Delta=\\{(u,v,w):0\\le u\\le 1,\\quad 0\\le v\\le 1,\\quad 0\\le w\\le 2\\}.\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial(u,v,w)}{\\partial(x,y,z)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial z} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial z} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial z}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\left(2\\right)(-1)^{3+3}\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\left(2\\right)\\left(\\left(-3\\right)\\cdot \\left(1\\right)-\\left(2\\right)\\cdot \\left(0\\right)\\right) \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial(x,y,z)}{\\partial(u,v,w)}=\\left(\\frac{\\partial(u,v,w)}{\\partial(x,y,z)}\\right)^{-1}=- \\frac{1}{6}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Perform the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iiint_R \\left(\\left(- 3 x + 2 y\\right) \\left(y - 2 z\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}V & =\\iiint_\\Delta \\left(u v\\right)\\cdot \\left|- \\frac{1}{6}\\right|\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\mathrm{d}v\\mathrm{d}w \\\\  & =\\iiint_\\Delta \\left(\\frac{u v}{6}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\mathrm{d}v\\mathrm{d}w \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\int_{0}^{1}\\int_{0}^{2}\\left(\\frac{u v}{6}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}w\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(\\left[\\frac{u v w}{6}\\right]_{w=0}^{w=2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(\\left(\\frac{u v \\left(2\\right)}{6}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{u v \\left(0\\right)}{6}\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(\\left(\\frac{u v}{3}\\right)-\\left(0\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(\\frac{u v}{3}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(\\left[\\frac{u v^{2}}{6}\\right]_{v=0}^{v=1}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(\\left(\\frac{u \\left(1\\right)^{2}}{6}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{u \\left(0\\right)^{2}}{6}\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(\\left(\\frac{u}{6}\\right)-\\left(0\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(\\frac{u}{6}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\left[\\frac{u^{2}}{12}\\right]_{u=0}^{u=1} \\\\  & =\\left(\\frac{\\left(1\\right)^{2}}{12}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{\\left(0\\right)^{2}}{12}\\right) \\\\  & =\\left(\\frac{1}{12}\\right)-\\left(0\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541334 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45c2c794-fa96-56ee-897b-6a7924f729cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-144" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541294} {:answer/id #uuid "5e7079ae-ca07-5029-bed0-98bf2758279f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541310} {:answer/id #uuid "7f871f55-3848-58d1-87a9-105664f12da9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541317} {:answer/id #uuid "9af31736-01f8-5259-af4f-3db984201269" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541325} {:answer/id #uuid "b5a62cf9-6bf3-5fb6-8756-053287095ab1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\sqrt{3} + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541333}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541310} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f004d4f-3fc8-5712-bdb7-94250c20150d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541278}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "cbecea42-79f4-5eda-a847-bcaa6ee8d720" :question/problem "Use the change of variables \n\n$$\nu=x^{2} + 4 y,\\quad v=x + 2 z,\\quad w=3 z\n$$\n\nto evaluate the triple integral\n\n$$\n\\iiint_R \\left(\\left(x^{2} + 4 y\\right) \\cos{\\left(x + 2 z \\right)}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}V,\n$$\n\n \nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z):1\\le x^{2} + 4 y\\le 3,\\quad \\frac{\\pi}{6}\\le x + 2 z\\le 2 \\pi,\\quad 1\\le z\\le 3\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uvw$-space to our region $R$ in the $xyz$-space.\n\nTo compute the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\text{ }dV={∭}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v,w),y(u,v,w),z(u,v,w))\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nNote that the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=x^{2} + 4 y,\\quad v=x + 2 z,\\quad w=3 z\n$$\n\ngives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}u(x,y,z) \\\\ v(x,y,z) \\\\ w(x,y,z)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo compute the required integral, we proceed in four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $R$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nOur domain in the $uvw$-space is\n\n$$\n\\Delta=\\{(u,v,w):1\\le u\\le 3,\\quad \\frac{\\pi}{6}\\le v\\le 2 \\pi,\\quad 3\\le w\\le 9\\}.\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial(u,v,w)}{\\partial(x,y,z)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial z} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial z} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial z}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 x & 4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\left(3\\right)(-1)^{3+3}\\begin{vmatrix}2 x & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\left(3\\right)\\left(\\left(2 x\\right)\\cdot \\left(0\\right)-\\left(4\\right)\\cdot \\left(1\\right)\\right) \\\\  & =-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial(x,y,z)}{\\partial(u,v,w)}=\\left(\\frac{\\partial(u,v,w)}{\\partial(x,y,z)}\\right)^{-1}=- \\frac{1}{12}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Perform the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iiint_R \\left(\\left(x^{2} + 4 y\\right) \\cos{\\left(x + 2 z \\right)}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}V & =\\iiint_\\Delta \\left(u \\cos{\\left(v \\right)}\\right)\\cdot \\left|- \\frac{1}{12}\\right|\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\mathrm{d}v\\mathrm{d}w \\\\  & =\\iiint_\\Delta \\left(\\frac{u \\cos{\\left(v \\right)}}{12}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\mathrm{d}v\\mathrm{d}w \\\\  & =\\int_{1}^{3}\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{2 \\pi}\\int_{3}^{9}\\left(\\frac{u \\cos{\\left(v \\right)}}{12}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}w\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{1}^{3}\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{2 \\pi}\\left(\\left[\\frac{u w \\cos{\\left(v \\right)}}{12}\\right]_{w=3}^{w=9}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{1}^{3}\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{2 \\pi}\\left(\\left(\\frac{u \\left(9\\right) \\cos{\\left(v \\right)}}{12}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{u \\left(3\\right) \\cos{\\left(v \\right)}}{12}\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{1}^{3}\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{2 \\pi}\\left(\\left(\\frac{3 u \\cos{\\left(v \\right)}}{4}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{u \\cos{\\left(v \\right)}}{4}\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{1}^{3}\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{2 \\pi}\\left(\\frac{u \\cos{\\left(v \\right)}}{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{1}^{3}\\left(\\left[\\frac{u \\sin{\\left(v \\right)}}{2}\\right]_{v=\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{v=2 \\pi}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{1}^{3}\\left(\\left(\\frac{u \\sin{\\left(\\left(2 \\pi\\right) \\right)}}{2}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{u \\sin{\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right) \\right)}}{2}\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{1}^{3}\\left(\\left(0\\right)-\\left(\\frac{u}{4}\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{1}^{3}\\left(- \\frac{u}{4}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\left[- \\frac{u^{2}}{8}\\right]_{u=1}^{u=3} \\\\  & =\\left(- \\frac{\\left(3\\right)^{2}}{8}\\right)-\\left(- \\frac{\\left(1\\right)^{2}}{8}\\right) \\\\  & =\\left(- \\frac{9}{8}\\right)-\\left(- \\frac{1}{8}\\right) \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541338 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "076da802-ebd4-5da6-989d-b4e5ee107e32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541276} {:answer/id #uuid "41536c9e-e5b7-5db2-82d2-6457fa4bfb50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "54" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541293} {:answer/id #uuid "946eea59-cb39-5110-93da-4da8429496e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541320} {:answer/id #uuid "9a9c3439-8be9-5d70-9591-b114a9dd46ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{3 \\sqrt{3}}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541323} {:answer/id #uuid "a7eb6120-e06c-502b-a15a-ded7ad89fd3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541330}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541320} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ac30ff6-c4fa-56e7-b428-f1de8fca1721" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541324}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "e65aaa3c-bfef-550f-8cdc-5c5c2d6c14c5" :question/problem "Use the change of variables \n\n$$\nu=x^{2} + 4 y,\\quad v=x + 2 z,\\quad w=3 z\n$$\n\nto evaluate the triple integral\n\n$$\n\\iiint_R \\left(\\left(x + 2 z\\right) \\cos{\\left(x^{2} + 4 y \\right)}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}V,\n$$\n\n \nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z):\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\le x^{2} + 4 y\\le \\frac{\\pi}{2},\\quad 1\\le x + 2 z\\le 2,\\quad 1\\le z\\le 3\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uvw$-space to our region $R$ in the $xyz$-space.\n\nTo compute the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\text{ }dV={∭}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v,w),y(u,v,w),z(u,v,w))\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nNote that the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=x^{2} + 4 y,\\quad v=x + 2 z,\\quad w=3 z\n$$\n\ngives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}u(x,y,z) \\\\ v(x,y,z) \\\\ w(x,y,z)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo compute the required integral, we proceed in four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $R$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nOur domain in the $uvw$-space is\n\n$$\n\\Delta=\\{(u,v,w):\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\le u\\le \\frac{\\pi}{2},\\quad 1\\le v\\le 2,\\quad 3\\le w\\le 9\\}.\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial(u,v,w)}{\\partial(x,y,z)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial z} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial z} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial z}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 x & 4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\left(3\\right)(-1)^{3+3}\\begin{vmatrix}2 x & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\left(3\\right)\\left(\\left(2 x\\right)\\cdot \\left(0\\right)-\\left(4\\right)\\cdot \\left(1\\right)\\right) \\\\  & =-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial(x,y,z)}{\\partial(u,v,w)}=\\left(\\frac{\\partial(u,v,w)}{\\partial(x,y,z)}\\right)^{-1}=- \\frac{1}{12}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Perform the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iiint_R \\left(\\left(x + 2 z\\right) \\cos{\\left(x^{2} + 4 y \\right)}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}V & =\\iiint_\\Delta \\left(v \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}\\right)\\cdot \\left|- \\frac{1}{12}\\right|\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\mathrm{d}v\\mathrm{d}w \\\\  & =\\iiint_\\Delta \\left(\\frac{v \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}}{12}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\mathrm{d}v\\mathrm{d}w \\\\  & =\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\int_{1}^{2}\\int_{3}^{9}\\left(\\frac{v \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}}{12}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}w\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\int_{1}^{2}\\left(\\left[\\frac{v w \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}}{12}\\right]_{w=3}^{w=9}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\int_{1}^{2}\\left(\\left(\\frac{v \\left(9\\right) \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}}{12}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{v \\left(3\\right) \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}}{12}\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\int_{1}^{2}\\left(\\left(\\frac{3 v \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}}{4}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{v \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}}{4}\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\int_{1}^{2}\\left(\\frac{v \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}}{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\left(\\left[\\frac{v^{2} \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}}{4}\\right]_{v=1}^{v=2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\left(2\\right)^{2} \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}}{4}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{\\left(1\\right)^{2} \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}}{4}\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\left(\\left(\\cos{\\left(u \\right)}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{\\cos{\\left(u \\right)}}{4}\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\left(\\frac{3 \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}}{4}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\left[\\frac{3 \\sin{\\left(u \\right)}}{4}\\right]_{u=\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{u=\\frac{\\pi}{2}} \\\\  & =\\left(\\frac{3 \\sin{\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right) \\right)}}{4}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{3 \\sin{\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right) \\right)}}{4}\\right) \\\\  & =\\left(\\frac{3}{4}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{3}{8}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541340 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "274826f8-5ee6-5553-bcdf-f924e9e3dc12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541289} {:answer/id #uuid "45f790a6-5bdd-5a23-8e33-6514f21d7fb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541295} {:answer/id #uuid "75202ae0-10b9-5c01-86bc-851a32c37874" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "44" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541313} {:answer/id #uuid "9cdf4172-38bd-54c7-b0af-051c53b46cfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541326} {:answer/id #uuid "d448f991-6e4c-5057-88e8-e3ae71348076" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541336}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541313} :answer-field/id #uuid "55e464bd-ee58-52ed-a62f-e6330cc3a34a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541300}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "ed8bddf2-150b-5447-8fa1-d8697f536efc" :question/problem "Use the change of variables \n\n$$\nu=x - \\frac{y}{4},\\quad v=\\frac{y}{4},\\quad w=\\frac{z}{2}\n$$\n\nto evaluate the triple integral\n\n$$\n\\iiint_R \\left(x - \\frac{y}{4} + \\frac{z}{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}V,\n$$\n\n \nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z):1\\le x - \\frac{y}{4}\\le 3,\\quad 1\\le \\frac{y}{4}\\le 3,\\quad 1\\le z\\le 2\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uvw$-space to our region $R$ in the $xyz$-space.\n\nTo compute the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\text{ }dV={∭}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v,w),y(u,v,w),z(u,v,w))\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nNote that the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=x - \\frac{y}{4},\\quad v=\\frac{y}{4},\\quad w=\\frac{z}{2}\n$$\n\ngives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}u(x,y,z) \\\\ v(x,y,z) \\\\ w(x,y,z)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo compute the required integral, we proceed in four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $R$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nOur domain in the $uvw$-space is\n\n$$\n\\Delta=\\{(u,v,w):1\\le u\\le 3,\\quad 1\\le v\\le 3,\\quad \\frac{1}{2}\\le w\\le 1\\}.\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial(u,v,w)}{\\partial(x,y,z)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial z} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial z} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial z}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & - \\frac{1}{4} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)(-1)^{3+3}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & - \\frac{1}{4} \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{4}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\left(\\left(1\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right)-\\left(- \\frac{1}{4}\\right)\\cdot \\left(0\\right)\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial(x,y,z)}{\\partial(u,v,w)}=\\left(\\frac{\\partial(u,v,w)}{\\partial(x,y,z)}\\right)^{-1}=8.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Perform the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iiint_R \\left(x - \\frac{y}{4} + \\frac{z}{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}V & =\\iiint_\\Delta \\left(u + w\\right)\\cdot \\left|8\\right|\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\mathrm{d}v\\mathrm{d}w \\\\  & =\\iiint_\\Delta \\left(8 u + 8 w\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\mathrm{d}v\\mathrm{d}w \\\\  & =\\int_{1}^{3}\\int_{1}^{3}\\int_{\\frac{1}{2}}^{1}\\left(8 u + 8 w\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}w\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{1}^{3}\\int_{1}^{3}\\left(\\left[8 u w + 4 w^{2}\\right]_{w=\\frac{1}{2}}^{w=1}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{1}^{3}\\int_{1}^{3}\\left(\\left(4 \\left(1\\right)^{2}\\right)-\\left(4 \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^{2}\\right)+\\left(8 u \\left(1\\right)\\right)-\\left(8 u \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{1}^{3}\\int_{1}^{3}\\left(\\left(4\\right)-\\left(1\\right)+\\left(8 u\\right)-\\left(4 u\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{1}^{3}\\int_{1}^{3}\\left(4 u + 3\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{1}^{3}\\left(\\left[v \\left(4 u + 3\\right)\\right]_{v=1}^{v=3}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{1}^{3}\\left(\\left(3 \\left(3\\right)\\right)-\\left(3 \\left(1\\right)\\right)+\\left(4 u \\left(3\\right)\\right)-\\left(4 u \\left(1\\right)\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{1}^{3}\\left(\\left(9\\right)-\\left(3\\right)+\\left(12 u\\right)-\\left(4 u\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\int_{1}^{3}\\left(8 u + 6\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  & =\\left[4 u^{2} + 6 u\\right]_{u=1}^{u=3} \\\\  & =\\left(4 \\left(3\\right)^{2}\\right)-\\left(4 \\left(1\\right)^{2}\\right)+\\left(6 \\left(3\\right)\\right)-\\left(6 \\left(1\\right)\\right) \\\\  & =\\left(36\\right)-\\left(4\\right)+\\left(18\\right)-\\left(6\\right) \\\\  & =44\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541346 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37a87cd5-635f-5714-9ff7-1501eac8f8a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/05/05a85c27c33421d67a198ab65111a484967eb8bf1ec97d5881b0b50c0b26c8ff.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541355} {:answer/id #uuid "54d432d4-57f5-50e0-a07b-4e0b563624ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/0d/0d6d817325324661cf7b0b3a73a89a8d63558bd90ae268c7598092d5a1354c49.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541360} {:answer/id #uuid "cff99e6c-e58d-55f1-933a-16641bf95e9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/f0/f06ac726fc0c602ad63a5ac830702dbb7bb01bc9516e8df4a3e83107d0afa1d6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541400} {:answer/id #uuid "de50e907-c0e5-59ab-b887-7778a4dcb99f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/e2/e2890e20881a7bc6c3f537f62305bbf4aa6b9b1de4264fb8139520c9940d0e92.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541409} {:answer/id #uuid "e2070a2a-7767-5ba0-b7cc-05836a7e3971" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/9b/9bef2a7540d3ae348165a601cffddcf32ddcfca7207bb31f14f9053438d39c28.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541411}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541360} :answer-field/id #uuid "c5bba0f6-32b6-5eda-9fcf-43279157826a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541394}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "08434fb0-6532-59e4-bcda-afba09f8c2fa" :question/problem "Which of the following shows the region in the $uv$-plane where the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}4 u - 12 \\\\ 2 \\left(v + 2\\right)^{2}\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nis (locally) orientation-reversing?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a transformation is (locally) orientation-reversing at the points where the Jacobian determinant is negative:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}<0\n$$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}4 u - 12 \\\\ 2 \\left(v + 2\\right)^{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} &=\\begin{vmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 v + 8\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ &=(4)\\cdot (4 v + 8)-(0)\\cdot (0) \\\\ &=16 v + 32.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the required regions, we solve the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16 v + 32 &<0 \\\\ v < -2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the equation\n\n$$\nv = -2\n$$\n\ndefines a horizontal line.\n\nTherefore, the region where the transformation is (locally) orientation-reversing must be the following:\n\n![](images/0d/0d6d817325324661cf7b0b3a73a89a8d63558bd90ae268c7598092d5a1354c49.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541347 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57964daf-2acf-57ba-b59c-295b8fceed9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/35/3514dfa39dddf1327e2d355ecfdf0c1a54596772554c49749e6f88c4f63e1c69.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541362} {:answer/id #uuid "af133e12-6645-589a-9628-434ecbaaaed3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/94/94f8fc7f53d269b8f902460bc29938d1bee5e71e9f8a4024e6916c9729cfe942.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541386} {:answer/id #uuid "af401e3c-68a4-5187-8578-6c3bd89fcc82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/a9/a9652984e1c261b065dca8d9ab1fae943b7f549c363201495fa2d86dace43964.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541387} {:answer/id #uuid "d35b5cc4-4666-5871-9f4b-3e03ebb0a54a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/dd/ddaffc1b9c44fc6aa22caac176f1fdd6e171c31e1246d884d25101473977fa9c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541403} {:answer/id #uuid "eb243a42-c920-525c-addf-01d6c2661a58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/e7/e7531367df6e086f961f6e4b39f382eebbb1d674f8708414059675fde5795be6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541414}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541403} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d482458-3681-59a2-a3cf-fe291c09a159" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541370}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "1669c7a6-5e4f-5ea0-88e1-7712fde23a58" :question/problem "Which of the following shows the region in the $uv$-plane where the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}2 v + \\left(u - 3\\right)^{2} + 4 \\\\ - 3 u - \\left(v + 2\\right)^{2} + 9\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nis (locally) orientation-reversing?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a transformation is (locally) orientation-reversing at the points where the Jacobian determinant is negative:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}<0\n$$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}2 v + \\left(u - 3\\right)^{2} + 4 \\\\ - 3 u - \\left(v + 2\\right)^{2} + 9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} &=\\begin{vmatrix}2 u - 6 & 2 \\\\ -3 & - 2 v - 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ &=(2 u - 6)\\cdot (- 2 v - 4)-(2)\\cdot (-3) \\\\ &=- 4 u v - 8 u + 12 v + 30.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the required regions, we solve the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}- 4 u v - 8 u + 12 v + 30 &<0 \\\\ \\left(u - 3\\right) \\left(v + 2\\right) > \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the solution $v > -2 + \\frac{3}{2 \\left(u - 3\\right)}$ for $u>3$ and $v < -2 + \\frac{3}{2 \\left(u - 3\\right)}$ for $u<3.$ At $u=3,$ the Jacobian is positive, so this line is excluded from the required region.\n\nNotice that the equation\n\n$$\nv = -2 + \\frac{3}{2 \\left(u - 3\\right)}\n$$\n\ndefines a hyperbola.\n\nTherefore, the region where the transformation is (locally) orientation-reversing must be the following:\n\n![](images/dd/ddaffc1b9c44fc6aa22caac176f1fdd6e171c31e1246d884d25101473977fa9c.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541352 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "222535a2-4caf-5d24-8c9b-b56cfc089a08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/d2/d20afed479d7bf650adc8540ba6f28f9d21243d7017ab3fe0691f5603078575e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541351} {:answer/id #uuid "30f473e9-a3c2-590b-817d-9c1f196951a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/53/5358c811168ad9ce8e801e22415864f34b5d694fa50e69aa03c352b7d153cfd5.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541353} {:answer/id #uuid "c2885d29-2182-5713-9c10-f79670914ca1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/6d/6d3dd3fffbd04ef723ec8bb0701747d5d7f973a23d2ecfdf0437f8827a6e0cec.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541392} {:answer/id #uuid "cf5a6394-0db1-54ff-8432-b11565760ab8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/6b/6bc5057212ab1c347102f5c09aa4d21eb9bb0f6215ed7294be4b30c127e90deb.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541398} {:answer/id #uuid "d29f05f9-483a-506e-af21-2a64161880a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/6f/6f964fd6850041d6454091d0232b5fc4866e8fec17c68d7e29f8a046fd455e2c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541402}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541398} :answer-field/id #uuid "39040f65-b728-5a51-bd54-b65202ef34c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541356}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2c2eb638-8c4b-5662-a604-688e503fe711" :question/problem "Which of the following shows the region in the $uv$-plane where the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}u + 3 \\\\ \\left(v + 1\\right)^{2}\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nis (locally) orientation-preserving?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a transformation is (locally) orientation-preserving at the points where the Jacobian determinant is positive:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}>0\n$$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}u + 3 \\\\ \\left(v + 1\\right)^{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} &=\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 v + 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ &=(1)\\cdot (2 v + 2)-(0)\\cdot (0) \\\\ &=2 v + 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the required regions, we solve the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 v + 2 &>0 \\\\ v > -1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the equation\n\n$$\nv = -1\n$$\n\ndefines a horizontal line.\n\nTherefore, the region where the transformation is (locally) orientation-preserving must be the following:\n\n![](images/6b/6bc5057212ab1c347102f5c09aa4d21eb9bb0f6215ed7294be4b30c127e90deb.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541357 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e5d9479-126c-53c4-a623-18e52a881365" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/89/898fd878de4c411294f1949a767f28c2b5d8b2f8c4f9096b5f78835fd51c31f7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541350} {:answer/id #uuid "58432077-1e38-53b0-ac66-cd774227ddf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/e2/e26d4947959fefd65cf852be709eaed2ac363225442686a5f160e02de1e798b3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541363} {:answer/id #uuid "9590b6ce-5d86-5e23-b1cd-3d744ff7719d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/a7/a77c173f49ff007692a1f040708adecbe65b7b035ce776faef93de1f8ce6019a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541377} {:answer/id #uuid "c702b198-4176-5491-be20-71307ad8580b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/a7/a7ba4a937a154e28f17d278