to the required region.\n\nNotice that the equation\n\n$$\nv = -1 + \\frac{3}{4 \\left(u + 3\\right)}\n$$\n\ndefines a hyperbola.\n\nTherefore, the region where the transformation is (locally) orientation-preserving must be the following:\n\n![](images/a7/a77c173f49ff007692a1f040708adecbe65b7b035ce776faef93de1f8ce6019a.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541361 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "675f8f01-4c56-5d4a-a654-9bcd0db9ac05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/26/26c6b06e7265268f7bebf6168a8c78757540cf0293ff4dd4ad05b789eb9fd40a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541367} {:answer/id #uuid "b246f7e9-f68f-5fc1-8278-87edbd99b3dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/8c/8ce7c030f900131fc3657c23518899642a6c2a2d85cfc133e55e5d7e57b6a0ff.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541388} {:answer/id #uuid "b3edee41-d23a-5b9b-8654-4f05dc12f80b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/1f/1f9b6cdb376451952b34f064c5ed296c5f0fee6c12ec2b7b3c85b0a616120ca4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541389} {:answer/id #uuid "d3fef0d7-a8a0-5d26-8b03-95cf3e30033c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/c5/c55116b6c9a7a78b548eaef6002dc56584ddf8498adb550335b3bf27593fb7ea.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541404} {:answer/id #uuid "f8f30f35-df0e-5743-ad3a-9d2361d8d8fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/23/23e1e36905e8fc966dfd473ac187e6480018a654086b3c9bdd82063227761816.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541415}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541404} :answer-field/id #uuid "a44962ff-6d21-5f24-bb46-bc557eac1492" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541380}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "565943af-a957-5402-9505-63da18eb789f" :question/problem "Which of the following shows the region in the $uv$-plane where the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\left(u + 3\\right)^{2} \\\\ 2 v + 2\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nis (locally) orientation-reversing?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a transformation is (locally) orientation-reversing at the points where the Jacobian determinant is negative:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}<0\n$$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\left(u + 3\\right)^{2} \\\\ 2 v + 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} &=\\begin{vmatrix}8 u + 24 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ &=(8 u + 24)\\cdot (2)-(0)\\cdot (0) \\\\ &=16 u + 48.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the required regions, we solve the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16 u + 48 &<0 \\\\ u < -3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the equation\n\n$$\nu = -3\n$$\n\ndefines a vertical line.\n\nTherefore, the region where the transformation is (locally) orientation-reversing must be the following:\n\n![](images/c5/c55116b6c9a7a78b548eaef6002dc56584ddf8498adb550335b3bf27593fb7ea.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541364 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "724de8f7-79a1-5698-8f05-517251248be1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/bc/bccf613be460b4765579cd916f63a6c216880214174583c134fc398a9a5f3809.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541371} {:answer/id #uuid "82acfdb9-c6e4-5a67-b65f-7ec1696341e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/e5/e5b61a928312936f111db2d8d3ae870bdb6c2cb0bb27a1ba12db333c0aa76cfa.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541373} {:answer/id #uuid "8fa52ab2-258a-5799-8dea-abbb50d3ed55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/61/61eb7087a9aa310143a93f0dd0cf549196c66536baa0570bb3b7158b934e38ff.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541375} {:answer/id #uuid "909033da-49b3-56e3-8b2d-b060b00f0eef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/55/55c4523390f0c74b41c7572e5160e3db9ef596061d1b8cd70bfd30a265de4161.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541376} {:answer/id #uuid "d92365d2-3a8f-5b47-8625-dbb8d48d1016" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/23/23b757a918d46889aa0786289dad81b089876b521c1f52cb94aa8c306cea284c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541405}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541375} :answer-field/id #uuid "9aff8968-d096-54f6-8a79-ed279c14f061" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541379}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "59add0cf-4e80-54d4-b7e4-f8be9314c117" :question/problem "Which of the following shows the region in the $uv$-plane where the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}2 v + \\left(u + 1\\right)^{2} + 2 \\\\ - u - \\left(v + 1\\right)^{2} - 1\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nis (locally) orientation-preserving?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a transformation is (locally) orientation-preserving at the points where the Jacobian determinant is positive:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}>0\n$$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}2 v + \\left(u + 1\\right)^{2} + 2 \\\\ - u - \\left(v + 1\\right)^{2} - 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} &=\\begin{vmatrix}2 u + 2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & - 2 v - 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ &=(2 u + 2)\\cdot (- 2 v - 2)-(2)\\cdot (-1) \\\\ &=- 4 u v - 4 u - 4 v - 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the required regions, we solve the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}- 4 u v - 4 u - 4 v - 2 &>0 \\\\ \\left(u + 1\\right) \\left(v + 1\\right) < \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the solution $v < -1 + \\frac{1}{2 \\left(u + 1\\right)}$ for $u>-1$ and $v > -1 + \\frac{1}{2 \\left(u + 1\\right)}$ for $u<-1.$ At $u=-1,$ the Jacobian is positive, so this line belongs to the required region.\n\nNotice that the equation\n\n$$\nv = -1 + \\frac{1}{2 \\left(u + 1\\right)}\n$$\n\ndefines a hyperbola.\n\nTherefore, the region where the transformation is (locally) orientation-preserving must be the following:\n\n![](images/61/61eb7087a9aa310143a93f0dd0cf549196c66536baa0570bb3b7158b934e38ff.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541368 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48f408a0-6e39-5b2c-9d7b-1e9430158db7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/d9/d9383071f1ee1de5f6a619559bebb5c2bc60f09e74655a476dc11981e26d8b93.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541358} {:answer/id #uuid "6759a9bf-0828-5f66-a722-fd710424a2b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/64/645c29d8beb5ddfe4c108002292a7fc13c6fc62dba4a6f616d2e4cbce3181278.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541366} {:answer/id #uuid "6cded118-0827-53b0-a109-b308dbdffd78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/44/44a052682a5fc6f18580bf3c3bea2835352972a195ebb4dbfda452c7163f538b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541369} {:answer/id #uuid "7b8c6549-87e1-5473-bf2f-c1b31ae4d655" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/1b/1bb0a60cf8676d84fb9ff02d4dc1ae0b429c6aa8ea3911e4846bd6b9470ca05c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541372} {:answer/id #uuid "adcebe86-8756-5934-805b-e2b9a4a06122" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/5b/5bc82f3c47998e71524755031882b38c2eee0f9f2f09871f6fdaab12e5ba3841.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541385}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541366} :answer-field/id #uuid "cbab2ee8-9f6e-5401-8a20-1f037631d0aa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541397}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6b68b81d-0d26-5a45-aadd-1f07bfe3d5e1" :question/problem "Which of the following shows the region in the $uv$-plane where the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}4 u + 12 \\\\ 4 \\left(v - 3\\right)^{2}\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nis (locally) orientation-preserving?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a transformation is (locally) orientation-preserving at the points where the Jacobian determinant is positive:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}>0\n$$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}4 u + 12 \\\\ 4 \\left(v - 3\\right)^{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} &=\\begin{vmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 8 v - 24\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ &=(4)\\cdot (8 v - 24)-(0)\\cdot (0) \\\\ &=32 v - 96.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the required regions, we solve the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}32 v - 96 &>0 \\\\ v > 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the equation\n\n$$\nv = 3\n$$\n\ndefines a horizontal line.\n\nTherefore, the region where the transformation is (locally) orientation-preserving must be the following:\n\n![](images/64/645c29d8beb5ddfe4c108002292a7fc13c6fc62dba4a6f616d2e4cbce3181278.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541390 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "370415d1-58c4-5284-bfae-31a0be8367d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/53/5389d4bb3047ce09fdd363b74f11656401529f5385409f693c18a1c20cac51ec.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541354} {:answer/id #uuid "4a4383ff-729c-5878-8348-4f2b0d1ad4b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/c6/c66e6dd0389d46178372b1cc1730b323671e6a7ea7010a8dc400866b63561409.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541359} {:answer/id #uuid "dc32f06a-61d1-5319-9f88-b0c254c6a451" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/44/44ca94fdc013bdefb282eb0b215303330a93bb537b0327ab94506e8ae85b7abc.png" :db/id #edb/ref 1759218654